GitWand
-------

  What            An external TypeScript engine for automatic git-conflict
                  resolution.
  Where in LCARS  `fleet/lib/fleet/conflict/` — the deterministic core
                  (pattern matching, hunk classification, the composite score)
                  was RE-IMPLEMENTED in pure Elixir from a reverse-engineering
                  study. No GitWand source, artifact or dependency ships here.
  Why re-coded    Audit verdict 6.5/10: an excellent deterministic core (8.5),
                  around dangerous peripheral layers — 12 format-aware resolvers
                  carrying 14 critical silent-data-loss paths, and an MCP surface
                  without containment. The decision was to keep the sane tier,
                  drop the rest, and put it behind our own jury loop, which
                  neutralises the data-loss motive: nothing is written without
                  being re-judged.
  Provenance      `fleet/CONFLICT-ENGINE-handoff.md` carries the full
                  chain — audit, what was kept, what was refused and why.

  The study itself lives outside this repository and stays there DELIBERATELY:
  it is reverse-engineering of someone else's product, reproducible by anyone
  who does the same work. We credit the origin; we do not ship four months of
  exploration of a third party's code.

  No licence text is reproduced here because no GitWand code is present. This
  entry is an attribution of ORIGIN, not a licence obligation being discharged —
  and it is written down precisely because the distinction stops being obvious
  once the prose that carried it has moved on.
